              "passage": "<p><strong>7.</strong> I started running because my doctor told me to, but now I cannot imagine a week without it.</p><p><strong>8.</strong> Our family always cooks plov on Fridays, and my grandmother still checks the rice herself.</p><p><strong>9.</strong> The bus to my office is crowded, so I listen to podcasts and forget about the noise.</p><p><strong>10.</strong> I learned to play the dutar at sixty, which proves it is never too late to begin.</p><p><strong>11.</strong> Working from home saved me two hours a day, but I miss chatting with colleagues.</p><p><strong>12.</strong> When I travel, I always buy a local cookbook instead of a souvenir.</p><p><strong>13.</strong> My phone tells me how many steps I take, and I try to beat yesterday's number.</p><p><strong>14.</strong> I volunteer at an animal shelter every Sunday; the dogs recognise me now.</p>",
